A||||5||Seanh||Gokart Questions and Ideas||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||12-13-2000||10:03 PM||||I got a wild idea today to build an armored gokart. Dont ask, but me and some friends play paintball about twice a month, pretty much anything goes. I would like to build a powerful, fully enclosed go kart, and need some ideas on things to do. First off, Would it be a real pain in the ass to have switchable 2/4 wheel drive? If I can do it, how? I was thinking stick shift kart maybe? Also, need some engine ideas, I would like at least about 25 HP, and would love more. I will probally try to Turbocharge it with a leaf blower.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Any one have any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||06:23 AM||||Yeah one idea comes to mind. Good luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>4 whel drive is not easy. I knew a guy tring to make a hydralic 4 wd??? I've played with some ideas but think i'll have to stick to 2 wheeling the mud. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||alpha||12-14-2000||10:05 AM||||I have a cart in the works which will be using a Honda 350cc motorcycle engine and a live axle. The manual trans is going to be great. <P>I would stay away with 4wd the cost is going to be stupid high and the traction you get with a live axle is quite good anyway.<P>You might consider making the enclosing panels removable leaving just a roll cage. driving a tank around is probably less then fun unless you are playing paintball.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://fiero.dhs.org/fiero/sig.jpg">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu">douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||12-14-2000||06:19 PM||||Yes, removeable body panels will be a must. I go to talking with a kid at school today about this idea, and... Well, how does a Quad4 4spd powered go-cart sound? I know someone who has a running Quad4 he is wanting to sell, and I could look around for a tranny. Probally only rear-wheel drive for now, but maybe a 4wd in the future. I also got to thinking, since this is a car engine, why not use some extras like heating a A/C, not really for any pratical purpose, just because it is a fun project to try. This would be one awesome cart. How much do Quad 4's weight in at? And, how much weight would I need to put up front to effectively counter it out? I will be a completely custom frame, so mounting issues wont be a problem.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I cant wait to get started on this one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-14-2000||06:43 PM||||Dude you need to build a dune buggy.<p>[This message has been edited by zeusrekning (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||afRaceR||12-14-2000||07:24 PM||||If you really want to put a car motor in one, I would try to find a Geo motor. A quad 4 would probably be too heavy to be any fun, the Geo motors are 3 cylinders and have stupid fuel economy, you would only need like a 2 gallon fuel tank, a real small radiator and a little transmission. <BR>Your probably only talking about a kart that ways 2 maybe 300 lbs without a motor anyways, you don't need that much power. The geo motor will also be alot easier to balance the weight in the car so one end isn't a lot heavier than the other.<BR>||||reg||1
